{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WenzlAOperator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WenzlAOperator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator.lrMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator.lrMultiplicity","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.lean#L53-L53","doc":"LR multiplicity `c^λ_{μν}` — the dimension of the multiplicity\nspace the block operator acts on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator.block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator.block","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.lean#L50-L50","doc":"`A^λ_{μν}(I)`: the `(μ, ν)`-block operator slot of interface `I`,\nindexed by `(λ, μ, ν, interface-label)`.  The codomain is a\nplaceholder; the numerical extract carries the endomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator","kind":"class","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.lean#L37-L53","doc":"**Wenzl A-operator** (`def:wenzl-A-operator`).\n\nPer Wenzl 1988 Sub-lemma 2.1, each inter-block interface generator\n`I = σ_{n₁}` decomposes per Wedderburn `(μ, ν)`-block as\n`A^λ_{μν}(I) ∈ End(V_μ ⊗ V_ν)^{⊕ c^λ_{μν}}`, with `c^λ_{μν}` the\nLittlewood–Richardson coefficient.  The class abstracts the operator\ndata as a map from `(λ, μ, ν, interface-label)` to the block-operator\nslot together with its LR multiplicity; the bilinear-system extract\nsupplies the concrete `End(V_μ ⊗ V_ν)^{⊕ c}` matrix entries. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:wenzl-A-operator","label":"def:wenzl-A-operator","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlPartition","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.lean#L34-L35","doc":"Partition (weakly-decreasing part list); doc-sibling local alias. ","signatureChunk":0}]}